  <section class="section mist" id="buyer-view">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker-num">03</span>What a buyer sees</p>
        <h2>From your records to a licensed dataset.</h2>
        <p>A plain picture of the steps between your systems and a buyer. Nothing is shared until the rights are clear and you approve the terms.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flow">
        <div class="flow-step reveal">
          <span class="flow-num">01</span>
          <h3>Your records</h3>
          <p>Customer threads, tickets, documents and deal notes as your team already keeps them.</p>
          <div class="sample-record"><b>Ticket 4821</b> &middot; Customer: [redacted]<br>Issue: billing sync failed<br>Resolution: re-authorised card<br>Handoff: [redacted] &middot; 14 Mar</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step reveal">
          <span class="flow-num">02</span>
          <h3>Rights and PII review</h3>
          <p>The data buyer reviews contracts, customer terms and personal information before anything is shared.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step reveal">
          <span class="flow-num">03</span>
          <h3>Scoped and de-identified</h3>
          <p>The data buyer removes or transforms personal identifiers, then reviews the copy again. Removing names alone does not make data anonymous.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step reveal">
          <span class="flow-num">04</span>
          <h3>Buyer sees the licensed scope</h3>
          <p>Scope, purpose and length of licence are set in the terms you approve. You approve every buyer.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="redact">
        <div class="redact-panel">
          <h3>In your systems</h3>
          <p class="redact-row"><span>Customer name</span><b>present</b></p>
          <p class="redact-row"><span>Email address</span><b>present</b></p>
          <p class="redact-row"><span>Issue</span><b>billing sync failed</b></p>
          <p class="redact-row"><span>Resolution</span><b>card re-authorised</b></p>
        </div>
        <div class="redact-panel buyer">
          <h3>In the licensed scope</h3>
          <p class="redact-row"><span>Customer name</span><b>[redacted]</b></p>
          <p class="redact-row"><span>Email address</span><b>[redacted]</b></p>
          <p class="redact-row"><span>Issue</span><b>billing sync failed</b></p>
          <p class="redact-row"><span>Resolution</span><b>card re-authorised</b></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="flow-note">Illustrative example, not a real record. Every dataset is reviewed on its own terms. <a href="trust.html">How we handle your data</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

